  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSides of triangle = 41, 21, 50\n\nBase = 21\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSemi-perimeter = (a + b + c) ÷ 2\n\nArea = √[s(s − a)(s − b)(s − c)]\n\nArea = (1 ÷ 2) × base × height\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ s = (41 + 21 + 50) ÷ 2 = 112 ÷ 2 = 56\n\n⇒ Area = √[56 × (56 − 41) × (56 − 21) × (56 − 50)]\n\n⇒ = √[56 × 15 × 35 × 6]\n\n⇒ = √[ (56 × 6) × (15 × 35) ]\n\n⇒ = √[336 × 525]\n\n⇒ = √[176400]\n\n⇒ Area = 420\n\n⇒ 420 = (1 ÷ 2) × 21 × height\n\n⇒ 420 = 21 × height ÷ 2\n\n⇒ height = (420 × 2) ÷ 21\n\n⇒ height = 840 ÷ 21 = 40\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 40.**",
